ria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Vegetarian","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Food, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"Food","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"z3REVRkZbxW9SUfy11mJPw","review_id":"q3t2XUvJgG1Hzs_IkoV4rQ","date":"2009-02-26T15:36:49","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9414777755737305,"text_excerpt":"I've only been to Cafe Bamboo for their grand opening night, but the food was absolutely delicious. We had to wait quite a while to have our order taken, and for the food to be brought to our table, but they were overwhelmed with the opening night crowd so I can't hold that against them. Their menu is almost completely vegan-friendly (there are a couple dishes with cheese), and is 100% vegetarian. While there are plenty of places around New Orleans to get a vegetarian meal, it's the only place where you don't have to ask a million questions to make sure it truly is vegetarian, because everything on the menu is edible for us herbivores."},{"business_id":"z3REVRkZbxW9SUfy11mJPw","review_id":"ogfaABAdFFixfAZFH9yxyA","date":"2009-08-20T01:34:52","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9379981160163879,"text_excerpt":"I am not vegan, but I love their food. Cafe Bamboo if the best vegan I've had in New Orleans and the Bourbon Chick'n Dinner is my fav. It reminds me a little of Red Bamboo in NYC, but don't tell the owner cause he doesn't like that too much. lol."},{"business_id":"z3REVRkZbxW9SUfy11mJPw","review_id":"DHpbCJqSVDD0uhWw__mftg","date":"2010-04-03T12:59:00","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9335209131240845,"text_excerpt":"This is place is awesome and a great find in New Orleans. Obviously it's a vegetarian restaurant but even if you aren't vegetarian, you will be glad you came to this place after eating all the delicious but unhealthy and animal product-laden food in New Orleans. We tried the Creole, Thai Curry, and Red beans and rice all with brown rice and they were all tasty. I would recommend the sampler, that way you can try three of them at the same time! They also have a full bar, wireless internet and an outdoor patio which is great when the weather is nice. It's very laid back and just a nice place to stop by for an hour or two."}],"visual":[]},"notebook_case":null}
